      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1376,
        624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Property Listing - Stale Lead Detector\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs every day at 8 AM to scan property listings from Google Sheets and calculate listing performance metrics against peer benchmarks. It refreshes a trend snapshot, filters for listings that need review and are not on cooldown, then sends eligible listings to Gemini for diagnosis. The parsed AI diagnosis is posted to Slack, and the alert is logged back to Google Sheets with an updated cooldown; a separate error path sends Slack alerts if the main workflow fails.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and configure the spreadsheet/ranges used for reading listings, refreshing the trend snapshot, and logging alerts/cooldowns.\n- Configure Slack credentials and select the channels or recipients for both listing alerts and workflow error alerts.\n- Provide the Gemini API key or credential used by the HTTP Request node and verify the request URL/body matches the desired Gemini model.\n- Confirm the daily schedule, review criteria, benchmark logic, and cooldown rules match the property listing process.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the code-based metrics, filter thresholds, Gemini prompt/request, Slack message format, and cooldown duration to match different markets or listing-review policies."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
